}

{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, thanks for reporting this. I found the cause: your account got locked after several failed sign-in attempts this morning, so the VPN (and Outlook/Teams) will keep refusing your password until the lock is cleared. I've asked a technician to unlock it, and you'll be able to sign in again once they approve. Until then, please don't keep retrying, because each try can extend the lock. After the unlock: 1) Before you sign in, check that the saved password is up to date on your phone's mail app and any other device. An old saved password is a common reason accounts keep locking. 2) Connect to the VPN and approve the Duo push on your phone. If it still says login failed after the unlock, or you're not sure of your password, reply and we'll arrange a password reset. A technician will phone you with the temporary password.",
  "internal_note": "Checked per KB-013/KB-001. Account status: locked, failed_login_count 5, vpn_access true, sign_in_blocked false. Duo enrolled (duo_push, Tom's phone). Sign-in logs: 5 failed_password attempts today, Fri 10:14-10:29 ET, app m365, corporate IP 203.0.113.10, New York, within usual hours (09:00-17:00). No mfa_denied, no hosting networks, no unusual locations. Previous VPN successes came from the usual residential IP 198.51.100.24 with Duo. Looks like a benign lockout (mistyped password or a saved credential), with no signs of compromise, so KB-031 does not apply. Password last set 2026-07-21, so this isn't a recent change. Queued unlock_account (approval id 1). No reset requested, because the user says he knows his password. Reset only if he asks for one, with the temp password given by callback. Escalate per KB-001 if it locks again within an hour after saved passwords are updated.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
